# Ui Component Research

## Purpose

Search approved UI libraries and existing project primitives before creating or redesigning interface patterns.

## When This Applies

- This rule applies when files matched by the glob are changed or generated.
- Use it when the task affects the behavior described by the purpose statement.

## Required Workflow

1. Search approved UI references for the specific pattern.
2. Reuse existing components before adding new ones.
3. Adapt patterns to project tokens and accessibility.
4. Document the inspiration source in notes or commit text.

## Standards

- Follow the existing project pattern before introducing a new one.
- Keep the implementation small, explicit, and easy to review.
- Prefer reusable project primitives, shared utilities, and documented conventions.
- Verify the change using the checks available in the project.

## Do Not

- Do not paste paid code without license confirmation.
- Do not introduce a new UI framework casually.
- Do not ignore mobile behavior.
- Do not use decorative motion that hurts readability.

## Verification Checklist

- The existing project pattern was inspected before changes were made.
- The implementation is scoped to the user request.
- Unsafe files, secrets, and unrelated changes are excluded.
- Applicable lint, typecheck, test, build, or validation commands were run when available.
- Any skipped or failed verification is reported clearly.

## Related Skills

- Use the matching `.cursor/skills/` workflow when one exists for this rule.
- When no matching skill exists, follow this rule directly and keep changes minimal, safe, and verifiable.
